It stays off for the agent. Its login cannot set flags on lab-mail,
and its replied tag means the agent replied, not you.

> Let's make two... Next and Later. This mirrors my Nirvana setup.

A correction to my last message first. I said lab-mail syncs every
folder (Patterns *) and that a new folder shows up on the other side
by itself. That is wrong. You asked for an explicit list in "Re:
[PATCH v3 0/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub"
[1], and v8 syncs only INBOX, Archive, and lists with Create None. So
new folders take a patch.

The patch is "[PATCH] jails/instances/lab-mail: Sync the Next and
Later folders" [2]. It applies on top of "[PATCH v8 0/9]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub" [3]. Dovecot
creates both folders, mbsync syncs them, and the spec makes the folder
the only state. You need to create Next and Later once in Fastmail's
web interface before the first sync, because mbsync creates no
folder.

> What will be the interface for making something as next or later in
> notmuch? Do I just tag it, and it moves? I think we've looked at
> something like this before, and that that's backwards... I need to move
> it into the folder, and derive the tag from the folder. I think?

Yes: move it, and derive the tag. We did look at the other way
around. "[PATCH] emacs: Archive notmuch mail by moving its file" [4]
moved a file when you tagged it archived. It was never applied.

Tagging first is backwards because it keeps the state in two places.
If the move fails, or the tag is set somewhere the hook does not run,
the tag and the folder disagree. A move made on Fastmail or on your
phone has no tag at all. With the folder as the only state, every
route is the same move, and the tag cannot drift. The spec says the
post-new hook sets next, later, and archived from the folder on every
run. A tag you add by hand lasts only until the next notmuch new.

In Emacs, that means one key each for INBOX, Next, Later, and Archive.
The command moves the message's file into that folder's cur/, keeping
the :2, flags and dropping mbsync's ,U= part of the name. Then it
runs notmuch new, so the tag shows up at once. Your next mbsync pushes
the move to lab-mail, and lab-mail pushes it to Fastmail. Moving it in
Fastmail works the same in reverse, and so does any other IMAP client.

The keys are your call. A prefix that matches your Nirvana shortcuts
seems natural to me. Tell me which you want.

The client side cannot land yet. mail-tag.sh, the Emacs command, and
flag sync all assume beastie reads ~/mail/pat@p7x.dev from lab-mail,
and today it reads the jj maildir, which has no Next or Later. That
work follows once the v8 series is applied and beastie's notmuch moves
over.

There is a conflict to fix at the same time. "[PATCH] dotfiles/notmuch:
Spec reading and sending through lab-mail" [5] makes beastie's mbsync
pull-only. A pull-only sync would undo every move you make locally,
so that spec has to change to two-way with Expunge Both, the way the
lab-mail spec already says.

